# DW3 Recompiled+ - public tree
#
# The launcher ships NO game code and NO game data. Everything derived from the player's own disc
# - the recompiled sources, the extracted game executables, the disc images themselves and every
# build artefact - is produced at run time and must never be committed. These rules enforce that;
# `verify_launcher.py` section X re-checks the patterns and the shipped engine's BIOS exception.

# --- build output: the tree root `build/` (generated sources, CMake tree) and Builds/ (the
#     finished regional runtimes the Play tab makes) --------------------------------
build/
Builds/
dist/
out/

# --- the player's own disc images and cards (never distributable) -----------------
# Root-level only: the save editor ships its own card-art folder under editor/, which must stay.
Discs/
discs/
/cards/
*.bin
*.cue
*.iso
*.chd
*.mdf
*.mds
*.img
*.mcr
*.mcd
*.mcs

# --- recompiler / generated C shards (derivative work) ---------------------------
# Root-level only: the engine's vendored libraries legitimately contain their own `generated/`
# source directories (rabbitizer), and those must still ship.
/generated/
*_full.c
*_full_*.c
*_dispatch.c
*_decls.h
*.ranges
bios-generated/

# --- runtime diagnostics ----------------------------------------------------------
psx_freeze_dump_*.json
psx_freeze_heartbeat.json
psx_last_run_report.json
/logs/
*.log

# --- python / env -----------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
launcher.json

# --- OS / editor junk -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# --- exceptions: the one BIOS image that is legal to ship ------------------------
# OpenBIOS is MIT (PCSX-Redux); its notice ships alongside as OpenBIOS.LICENSE. The bundled engine
# needs it so the player only ever has to supply a disc, so it is deliberately tracked despite the
# broad `*.bin` rule above.
!engine/framework/bios/openbios.bin
!engine/framework/bios/*.LICENSE

# --- documentation screenshots -----------------------------------------------------
# The README embeds its screenshots from GitHub's attachment store, so these PNGs are
# kept out of version control. They stay on disk so the owner can re-upload them.
docs/images/

# placeholder artwork kept aside during re-skinning; not shipped
*.bak
*.bak-*
